      "text": "I've logged the run as anomalous. The likely cause is a seal leak (a process fault), and I've recommended calling a human.\n\n- **What's wrong:** Once growth started, exhaust O2 went up by about 5–6 ppm every 120 s. Through the ramp it had stayed near 5 ppm, and it was 4.4 ppm at t=2640 s.\n- **What looks normal:** Ar flow holds at about 100 sccm, matching the setpoint, so the flow controller isn't the problem. Temperature holds at 750 °C with normal heater power.\n- **What's not confirmed:** This furnace has no pressure gauge, so I can't fully rule out an exhaust blockage or check the growth atmosphere the protocol requires. Tube pressure readings or a leak check on the seals would settle it.\n- **Science:** No characterization yet. If the O2 rise continues, any result from this run probably won't count as evidence about the recipe."
     }
